<!-- A texture as it is, with texels below half alpha discarded: Urho3D's
     Unlit with the texture's alpha cutting holes rather than being ignored
     or blended through. What is not part of the voxel world is drawn with
     it in both Luanti clients: entities, whose textures are full of holes,
     and an item's picture -- a plant, a tool, a sapling -- opaque where the
     picture is and not there at all where it is not, which is what
     use_texture_alpha = "clip" means for a node. CoreData has DiffUnlit
     (alpha ignored, so the holes are black) and DiffUnlitAlpha (blended,
     so a picture that is mostly holes is a ghost), and neither is this. -->
<technique vs="Unlit" ps="Unlit" psdefines="DIFFMAP ALPHAMASK">
    <pass name="base" />
</technique>
